WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.460
IELTS 20 published by Cambridge University Press and Assessment 2025. This recording

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.080
is copyright.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:19.360
Test 1. This is the IELTS listening test. You will hear a number of different recordings

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:25.200
and you will have to answer questions on what you hear. There will be time for you to read

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:31.740
the instructions and questions and you will have a chance to check your work. All the

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:40.160
recordings will be played once only. The test is in four parts. At the end of the test you

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:47.080
will be given 10 minutes to transfer your answers to an answer sheet.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:01:01.799
Now turn to part 1. Part 1. You will hear a woman asking a friend for restaurant recommendations.

00:01:01.799 --> 00:01:26.199
Next you have some time to look at questions 1 to 4.

00:01:26.199 --> 00:01:33.800
Now listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 4.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:39.080
I've been meaning to ask you for some advice about restaurants. I need to book somewhere

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:44.480
to celebrate my sister's 30th birthday and I liked the sound of that place you went to

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.440
for your mum's 50th.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:51.680
The Junction. Yeah, I'd definitely recommend that for a special occasion. We had a great

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.120
time there. Everyone really enjoyed it.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.879
Where is it again? I can't remember.

00:01:57.879 --> 00:02:02.400
It's on Grayson Street, only about a two-minute walk from the station.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:08.000
Oh, that's good. I'd prefer not to have to drive anywhere. But I don't want to have to

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.800
walk too far either.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:16.639
Yes, the location's perfect, but that's not necessarily why I'd recommend it. The food's

00:02:16.639 --> 00:02:24.600
amazing. If you like fish, it's probably the best restaurant in town for that. It's always

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:30.880
really fresh and there are lots of interesting dishes to choose from. But all the food is

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.160
good there.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.759
Is it really expensive?

00:02:34.759 --> 00:02:40.880
It's certainly not cheap, but for a special occasion I think it's fine. It's got a great

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:47.679
atmosphere and before dinner you can go up on the roof and have a drink. It's really

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:54.720
nice up there, but you need to book. It's very popular as the views are spectacular.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:03:01.440
Sounds good. So that's definitely a possibility then. Is there anywhere else you can think

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.639
of?

00:03:03.639 --> 00:03:07.479
If you want somewhere a bit less formal, then you could try Paloma.

00:03:07.479 --> 00:03:10.360
Where's that? I haven't heard of it.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:15.919
No, it's quite new. It's only been open a few months, but it's got a great reputation

00:03:15.919 --> 00:03:21.119
already. It's in a really beautiful old building on Bow Street.

00:03:21.119 --> 00:03:26.160
Oh, I think I know where you mean. Right beside the cinema?

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:32.600
Yes, that's it. I've only been there a couple of times, but I was really impressed. The

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:39.240
chef used to work at Don Felipe's apparently. I was really sorry when that closed down.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.279
So is all the food they serve Spanish then?

00:03:42.279 --> 00:03:48.160
Yes. You can get lots of small dishes to share, which always works really well if you're

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.000
in a group.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.080
Worth thinking about.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:57.880
Yes. There's a lively atmosphere and the waiters are really friendly. The only thing is that

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.800
you need to pay a £50 deposit to book a table.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:06.360
A lot of restaurants are doing that these days. I should have a look at the menu to

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:11.720
check there's a good choice of vegetarian dishes. A couple of my friends have stopped

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:13.399
eating meat.

00:04:13.399 --> 00:04:20.399
Not sure. I'd say the selection of those would be quite limited.

00:04:20.399 --> 00:04:26.600
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions five

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:27.200
to ten.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:05:01.720
Now listen and answer questions five to ten.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:08.720
I've just thought of another idea. Have you been to the Audley?

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:13.720
No, don't think I've heard of it. How's it spelt?

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:22.720
A-U-D-L-E-Y. You must have heard of it. There's been a lot about it in the press.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:28.720
I don't tend to pay much attention to that kind of thing. So where is it exactly?

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:33.720
It's in that hotel near Baxter Bridge on the top floor.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.720
Oh, the views would be incredible from up there.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:43.720
Yeah, I'd love to go. I can't think of the chef's name, but she was a judge on that TV

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:48.720
cookery show recently, and she's written a couple of cookery books.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.720
Oh, Angela Frain.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:56.720
That's the one. Anyway, it's had excellent reviews from all the newspapers.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:00.720
That would be a memorable place for a celebration.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:04.720
Definitely. Obviously it's worth going there just for the view,

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:08.720
but the food is supposed to be really special.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:12.720
She only likes cooking with local products, doesn't she?

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:17.720
Yes. Everything at the restaurant has to be sourced within a short distance,

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:21.720
and absolutely nothing flown in from abroad.

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:24.720
I imagine it's really expensive, though.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:31.720
Well, you could go for the set lunch. That's quite reasonable for a top-class restaurant.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:37.720
Thirty pounds a head. In the evening, I think it'd be more like fifty pounds.

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:42.720
At least that, I should think. But I'm sure everyone would enjoy it.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:48.720
It's not the kind of place you leave feeling hungry, though, is it? With tiny portions?

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:54.720
No, the reviews I've read didn't mention that. I imagine they'd be average.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.720
Well, that's all great. Thanks so much.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:23.720
Thank you for watching!

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:53.720
Please subscribe to my channel!

